{
  "semantics": {
    "attributes": {
      "final": {},
      "header": {}
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "For remote access, Spring JMX module offers two "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "FactoryBean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " implementations inside the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "org.springframework.jmx.support"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " package for creating both server- and client-side connectors."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To have Spring JMX create, start, and expose a JSR-160 "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JMXConnectorServer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", you can use the following configuration:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<bean id=\"serverConnector\" class=\"org.springframework.jmx.support.ConnectorServerFactoryBean\"/>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ConnectorServerFactoryBean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " creates a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JMXConnectorServer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " bound to "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "service:jmx:jmxmp://localhost:9875"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "serverConnector"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " bean thus exposes the local "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MBeanServer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to clients through the JMXMP protocol on localhost, port 9875. Note that the JMXMP protocol is marked as optional by the JSR 160 specification. Currently, the main open-source JMX implementation, MX4J, and the one provided with the JDK do not support JMXMP."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To specify another URL and register the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JMXConnectorServer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " itself with the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MBeanServer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", you can use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "serviceUrl"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ObjectName"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " properties, respectively, as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<bean id=\"serverConnector\"\n\t\tclass=\"org.springframework.jmx.support.ConnectorServerFactoryBean\">\n\t<property name=\"objectName\" value=\"connector:name=rmi\"/>\n\t<property name=\"serviceUrl\"\n\t\t\tvalue=\"service:jmx:rmi://localhost/jndi/rmi://localhost:1099/myconnector\"/>\n</bean>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ObjectName"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " property is set, Spring automatically registers your connector with the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MBeanServer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " under that "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ObjectName"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". The following example shows the full set of parameters that you can pass to the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "ConnectorServerFactoryBean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " when creating a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JMXConnector"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ":"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<bean id=\"serverConnector\"\n\t\tclass=\"org.springframework.jmx.support.ConnectorServerFactoryBean\">\n\t<property name=\"objectName\" value=\"connector:name=iiop\"/>\n\t<property name=\"serviceUrl\"\n\t\tvalue=\"service:jmx:iiop://localhost/jndi/iiop://localhost:900/myconnector\"/>\n\t<property name=\"threaded\" value=\"true\"/>\n\t<property name=\"daemon\" value=\"true\"/>\n\t<property name=\"environment\">\n\t\t<map>\n\t\t\t<entry key=\"someKey\" value=\"someValue\"/>\n\t\t</map>\n\t</property>\n</bean>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Note that, when you use a RMI-based connector, you need the lookup service ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "tnameserv"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "rmiregistry"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") to be started in order for the name registration to complete."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jmx-jsr160-server",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Server-side Connectors"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To create an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MBeanServerConnection"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " to a remote JSR-160-enabled "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MBeanServer"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", you can use the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MBeanServerConnectionFactoryBean"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<bean id=\"clientConnector\" class=\"org.springframework.jmx.support.MBeanServerConnectionFactoryBean\">\n\t<property name=\"serviceUrl\" value=\"service:jmx:rmi://localhost/jndi/rmi://localhost:1099/jmxrmi\"/>\n</bean>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jmx-jsr160-client",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Client-side Connectors"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "JSR-160 permits extensions to the way in which communication is done between the client and the server. The examples shown in the preceding sections use the mandatory RMI-based implementation required by the JSR-160 specification (IIOP and JRMP) and the (optional) JMXMP. By using other providers or JMX implementations (such as "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MX4J"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "http://mx4j.sourceforge.net"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") you can take advantage of protocols such as SOAP or Hessian over simple HTTP or SSL and others, as the following example shows:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "<bean id=\"serverConnector\" class=\"org.springframework.jmx.support.ConnectorServerFactoryBean\">\n\t<property name=\"objectName\" value=\"connector:name=burlap\"/>\n\t<property name=\"serviceUrl\" value=\"service:jmx:burlap://localhost:9874\"/>\n</bean>"
              }
            ],
            "language": "xml",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "In the preceding example, we used MX4J 3.0.0. See the official MX4J documentation for more information."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "section",
        "id": "jmx-jsr160-protocols",
        "level": 1,
        "roles": [],
        "title": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "JMX over Hessian or SOAP"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "outline": null,
    "title": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "value": "Using JSR-160 Connectors"
      }
    ]
  }
}
